WEBVTT

02:31.901 --> 02:33.528
Give Sarah my love.

03:06.102 --> 03:07.270
...multiple lacerations.

03:10.231 --> 03:12.150
My daughter, she's five years old.

03:29.626 --> 03:31.878
Hey. It's okay.

03:32.378 --> 03:34.088
You're in the hospital.

03:36.424 --> 03:38.218
Are you in pain?

03:39.093 --> 03:40.386
We can give you something.

03:43.932 --> 03:47.310
Ellie! Ellie!

03:52.941 --> 03:53.942
Here.

03:55.401 --> 03:56.694
It's okay.

06:01.736 --> 06:04.363
And how would you rate your pain?
Scale of one to ten?

06:04.364 --> 06:06.324
- Nothing. Zero.
- Zero.

06:07.492 --> 06:08.993
Can't ask for much more than that.

06:10.036 --> 06:12.372
Okay. One last PFT.

06:16.042 --> 06:17.042
Look at that.

06:17.043 --> 06:18.294
Yeah.

06:18.961 --> 06:19.961
Alright.

06:19.962 --> 06:21.130
Today's the day.

06:22.131 --> 06:23.548
- So, can I just--
- Almost.

06:23.549 --> 06:26.094
I just need you to see one more person,
then you're good to go.

06:30.556 --> 06:32.558
Oh, for fuck's sake.

06:34.227 --> 06:36.311
- How are you doing?
- Fine.

06:36.312 --> 06:38.563
If you say it that fast,
it kind of implies you're not.

06:38.564 --> 06:39.899
Okay, ask me again.

06:40.775 --> 06:41.984
How are you doing, Ellie?

06:43.569 --> 06:44.653
Give me a moment.

06:44.654 --> 06:47.656
It's really complicated
'cause, you know, feelings.

06:47.657 --> 06:49.074
Okay.

06:49.075 --> 06:51.577
Oh, come on, man,
I've been stuck in here since...

06:55.581 --> 06:58.125
Yeah, I miss him.
He meant a lot to me.

06:58.126 --> 07:00.169
So, yeah. Upset and sad.

07:00.795 --> 07:02.046
Of course.

07:02.588 --> 07:04.965
But I was actually wondering
about New Year's Eve.

07:04.966 --> 07:07.717
You two got into it at the dance.

07:07.718 --> 07:09.512
Was that the last time you spoke to him?

07:12.849 --> 07:13.850
Yeah.

07:15.101 --> 07:18.270
When I got home, he was on the porch,

07:18.271 --> 07:22.024
and I should've talked to him,
but I didn't.

07:23.025 --> 07:26.069
- Do you regret that?
- Yeah, of course.

07:26.070 --> 07:32.826
But your final moment with someone
doesn't define your whole time with them.

07:32.827 --> 07:35.288
It shouldn't, but it often does.

07:37.874 --> 07:40.668
In my last moment with Joel, he said he

07:41.794 --> 07:42.920
wronged you.

07:43.921 --> 07:45.047
Maybe bad.

07:49.051 --> 07:51.429
What is it that he said that he did?

07:52.430 --> 07:54.932
Well, that's the thing.
It didn't really make sense.

07:55.850 --> 07:57.810
He said, "I saved her."

08:00.354 --> 08:01.856
He saved me a lot of times.

08:02.523 --> 08:05.818
Yeah, I would think so.
But that's not wronging someone.

08:07.278 --> 08:08.279
That's weird.

08:09.530 --> 08:10.948
No idea what he meant.

08:12.283 --> 08:14.785
I don't feel wronged.

08:16.704 --> 08:18.246
Man, I wish I could have
let him off the hook

08:18.247 --> 08:20.541
for whatever it was he was talking about.

08:22.543 --> 08:26.130
I guess I'll have to let myself
off the hook for that.

08:28.299 --> 08:29.675
Well, you really are doing good.

08:31.385 --> 08:36.473
Shit, if everyone were as healthy as you,
what would I do for weed and booze?

08:36.474 --> 08:38.642
I wouldn't worry, Gail,
there's still a lot of fucked up people

08:38.643 --> 08:40.101
- in this town.
- Yeah.

08:40.102 --> 08:41.854
But not you, though.

12:40.426 --> 12:41.510
Ellie?

12:45.389 --> 12:46.557
Fuck.

12:51.854 --> 12:53.731
Yeah, I'm coming.

13:08.454 --> 13:10.456
I went to the hospital.

13:11.457 --> 13:13.333
When'd they let you out?

13:13.334 --> 13:16.003
- Thirty minutes ago.
- Nice.

13:17.254 --> 13:18.714
They made me talk to Gail.

13:24.345 --> 13:25.554
I never said--

13:26.305 --> 13:28.473
I should have said thank you

13:28.474 --> 13:30.392
for all those times you came to visit.

13:31.227 --> 13:33.478
That's okay.
You would have done the same for me.

13:33.479 --> 13:36.190
- Yeah, maybe not as often.
- Yeah, no, probably not.

13:38.442 --> 13:39.652
I made you cookies.

13:40.778 --> 13:42.695
- Just 'cause?
- No.

13:42.696 --> 13:44.532
This is a peace offering.

13:47.076 --> 13:48.869
Because I'm about to make you angry.

13:54.208 --> 13:55.709
In the hospital,

13:57.086 --> 14:00.548
when you asked me about that day,

14:01.590 --> 14:04.385
I told you I didn't learn anything useful.

14:06.220 --> 14:07.680
That wasn't true.

14:09.849 --> 14:13.727
I know most of their names,
and I know where they're from.

14:14.728 --> 14:17.730
Please, just listen.
The doctors told me not to upset you.

14:17.731 --> 14:19.816
- I don't give a fuck.
- And I knew that if I told you

14:19.817 --> 14:21.609
where they were,
you'd just start pulling your tubes out

14:21.610 --> 14:23.486
and crawling on your hands
and knees to get there.

14:23.487 --> 14:25.406
I don't give a fuck.

14:26.490 --> 14:30.202
You cost us time. You let them get away.

14:32.872 --> 14:34.706
First of all,

14:34.707 --> 14:37.417
this town was wreckage
and funerals for weeks.

14:37.418 --> 14:39.836
Nobody was gonna go after anyone.

14:39.837 --> 14:42.297
And then it occurred to me,
if you wanna find someone,

14:42.298 --> 14:44.967
and the only thing you know about them
is where they're gonna end up.

14:47.595 --> 14:49.305
Maybe let them get there.

14:57.938 --> 14:59.565
I loved him too, you know.

15:39.188 --> 15:41.357
Okay, let's start with names.

15:42.566 --> 15:45.652
The dark-haired guy was Manny.
The other guy was Owen.

15:45.653 --> 15:47.487
The girl with the dark hair
and the bald one,

15:47.488 --> 15:49.364
one of them's named Nora.
I'm not sure which.

15:49.365 --> 15:50.699
The girl with the braid?

15:51.825 --> 15:52.910
Abby.

15:53.452 --> 15:54.828
Abby.

15:57.790 --> 15:59.041
Where are they from?

16:00.042 --> 16:01.669
I saw a patch on a backpack.

16:03.087 --> 16:05.255
Yellow triangle, wolf's head,

16:06.423 --> 16:08.508
and the letters W-L-F.

16:08.509 --> 16:12.220
And then, I remembered a story Eugene
told me from back when he was a Firefly.

16:12.221 --> 16:13.888
He said that there were
these small regional groups

16:13.889 --> 16:15.348
in the West all trying to fight FEDRA,

16:15.349 --> 16:18.351
and how stupid it was
that they didn't just join together.

16:18.352 --> 16:22.231
One of those groups was
the Washington Liberation Front.

16:24.608 --> 16:26.275
Out of Seattle.

16:26.276 --> 16:28.361
W-L-F. Wolf.

16:28.362 --> 16:29.571
Fucking morons.

16:30.864 --> 16:33.157
- Did he say how small they were?
- No.

16:33.158 --> 16:35.368
But seeing as how no one's
ever mentioned them since,

16:35.369 --> 16:37.579
I'm guessing small enough
for us to handle.

16:39.707 --> 16:41.040
Who else knows?

16:41.041 --> 16:42.584
Just us.

16:44.837 --> 16:47.172
I wasn't gonna tell anyone before you.

17:06.900 --> 17:08.277
So, now what?

17:21.915 --> 17:22.958
Well?

17:24.043 --> 17:25.460
I gotta think about this.

17:25.461 --> 17:27.754
Think about what?
Let's fucking get these guys.

17:27.755 --> 17:29.839
Ellie, it ain't that simple.

17:29.840 --> 17:31.425
The town is still recovering.

17:32.009 --> 17:33.593
- So are you.
- We get where you're coming from--

17:33.594 --> 17:36.304
No, we don't get where you're coming from.
I don't get where you're coming from.

17:36.305 --> 17:38.014
If it had been you,
Joel would be halfway to Seattle

17:38.015 --> 17:39.932
- before the sun came up.
- He'd be halfway to Seattle

17:39.933 --> 17:41.310
to save my life.

17:42.019 --> 17:43.936
But when we lost people, no.

17:43.937 --> 17:46.064
It would just break him
like it was his fault.

17:46.065 --> 17:47.523
I saw that time and time again.

17:47.524 --> 17:49.318
And don't talk to me
like I didn't know him.

17:50.235 --> 17:51.445
He was my brother.

17:57.159 --> 18:00.704
Listen, I'm not sayin'
you shouldn't do this.

18:01.705 --> 18:03.247
But if we're gonna put a posse together,

18:03.248 --> 18:05.666
we gotta do it right,
which means taking it to Maria.

18:05.667 --> 18:07.919
Yes, it's fuckin' necessary.

18:07.920 --> 18:10.838
She's gonna want a council meeting,
open it up to the town.

18:10.839 --> 18:13.050
Everyone who wants
to get heard gets heard.

18:14.259 --> 18:15.677
But you'll back us, right?

18:16.512 --> 18:17.805
Of course, I will.

18:21.266 --> 18:22.351
Come here.

18:28.774 --> 18:31.651
And you, you hold out
information on me again,

18:31.652 --> 18:34.196
you got rendering detail for a month.

18:36.448 --> 18:37.449
Alright.

18:41.495 --> 18:42.496
Ellie.

18:45.541 --> 18:47.918
We buried our dead
ten miles south of town.

18:48.752 --> 18:50.295
If you want to visit him.

18:53.048 --> 18:54.967
When we're on our way to Seattle.

19:51.815 --> 19:52.900
Well?

19:54.443 --> 19:57.695
"No one following.
All clear. Keep moving."

19:57.696 --> 19:59.113
Good.

19:59.114 --> 20:02.117
Once we get resettled,
I'll teach you to whistle.

20:05.329 --> 20:07.539
Why can't you tell me where we're going?

20:08.123 --> 20:09.708
'Cause we don't know yet.

20:10.751 --> 20:12.793
I've told you the reason we're going.

20:12.794 --> 20:16.881
I know, but why can't
she just keep us safe?

20:16.882 --> 20:18.258
The Prophet?

20:19.635 --> 20:23.471
She's been dead ten years, Constance.
I wouldn't count on her to help.

20:23.472 --> 20:26.265
But Ezra said the Prophet is eternal.

20:26.266 --> 20:29.061
Well, she is, in a way.

20:29.811 --> 20:31.270
A prophet isn't magic.

20:31.271 --> 20:34.857
They're just people that see
truths hidden from others

20:34.858 --> 20:37.402
and share that truth,
no matter what the cost.

20:38.570 --> 20:40.571
So it was with our Prophet.

20:40.572 --> 20:42.198
So it was.

20:42.199 --> 20:44.575
That's how we keep her spirit alive.

20:44.576 --> 20:49.706
Follow her words, we obey her teachings,
but we keep ourselves safe.

20:53.418 --> 20:55.671
Then, can I have a hammer?

20:59.341 --> 21:00.342
Alright.

21:03.553 --> 21:06.389
Tell me, you feel safer?

21:06.390 --> 21:07.641
Yes.

21:08.642 --> 21:10.018
Good.

21:10.686 --> 21:12.687
Understand, what we're giving you now,

21:12.688 --> 21:15.357
will keep you far, far safer
than a hammer.

21:17.943 --> 21:19.361
Distance.

21:20.570 --> 21:21.863
From home.

21:22.281 --> 21:23.532
From war.

21:34.835 --> 21:36.295
Take cover! Go!

21:53.562 --> 21:54.730
Demons?

21:56.732 --> 21:57.941
Wolves.

22:01.153 --> 22:02.153
Alright.

22:02.154 --> 22:04.114
Good, but rotate. More.

22:04.573 --> 22:07.658
Now, the right side. Just the right side.

22:07.659 --> 22:08.993
Come on, man, that side hurts more.

22:08.994 --> 22:10.911
I noticed.

22:10.912 --> 22:12.080
- Come on.
- Okay.

22:13.540 --> 22:14.790
Harder.

22:14.791 --> 22:16.125
Harder! Let's go!

22:16.126 --> 22:17.461
Last five.

22:19.963 --> 22:22.465
There it is, okay. Done for the day.

22:22.466 --> 22:23.675
Okay.

22:25.010 --> 22:26.385
So, what'd you think?

22:26.386 --> 22:27.803
Well, for someone who sat on their ass

22:27.804 --> 22:30.348
for three months,
I'm pleasantly surprised.

22:30.349 --> 22:32.308
- Yeah?
- Push-ups?

22:32.309 --> 22:34.435
Yeah, and crunches
when they weren't looking.

22:34.436 --> 22:36.312
Yeah, that'll do it.

22:36.313 --> 22:38.647
A few more weeks, and you'll be right back
to where you were before.

22:38.648 --> 22:40.274
Nice.

22:40.275 --> 22:42.151
Which is 80% of where you
should have been.

22:42.152 --> 22:44.071
Whatever. Fuck you.

22:47.366 --> 22:50.494
So, I heard you're on the council now.

22:50.994 --> 22:51.995
Yep.

22:53.246 --> 22:55.332
So, you know about the meeting coming up?

22:56.917 --> 22:58.293
I know about the meeting coming up.

23:00.379 --> 23:02.255
Can I count on you?

23:04.257 --> 23:05.800
I can't discuss upcoming votes.

23:05.801 --> 23:07.927
Seriously? It's me.

23:07.928 --> 23:09.178
I know.

23:09.179 --> 23:10.971
Dude, you were there.

23:10.972 --> 23:12.474
I know that too.

23:13.517 --> 23:14.518
Gotta go.

23:16.186 --> 23:17.521
Oh, my God.

23:19.147 --> 23:20.856
Ellie.

23:20.857 --> 23:23.943
The council won't make up their mind
until we hear people speak.

23:23.944 --> 23:25.986
So, here's a little advice.

23:25.987 --> 23:28.531
Organize your thoughts, write them down,

23:28.532 --> 23:30.116
and then read 'em out loud tomorrow.

23:30.117 --> 23:31.867
Okay, yeah, 'cause I'm stupid.

23:31.868 --> 23:33.870
'Cause you're angry, Ellie.

23:35.163 --> 23:36.915
And no one's gonna vote for angry.

23:44.840 --> 23:47.258
Which is why I keep
saying we need to invest

23:47.259 --> 23:50.052
more in turkeys and less in chickens.

23:50.053 --> 23:53.305
And that brings me back
to my earlier point about corn.

23:53.306 --> 23:55.474
Corn, some of you have heard me say,

23:55.475 --> 23:59.228
is not the easiest crop to grow,
but it is among the fastest.

23:59.229 --> 24:02.148
You can plot a graph
that shows ease and resources

24:02.149 --> 24:04.024
versus time to harvest and get a li--

24:04.025 --> 24:07.529
Scott, I'm sorry,
but we gotta keep you on target here.

24:08.947 --> 24:11.031
But it's an open meeting.
The bylaws say that--

24:11.032 --> 24:12.575
Maybe we should stick
to what everyone else

24:12.576 --> 24:14.202
came here to discuss.

24:14.786 --> 24:17.204
I don't really have an opinion
on the Seattle thing.

24:17.205 --> 24:19.124
Okay. Thank you.

24:20.208 --> 24:21.376
So, that was Scott.

24:22.252 --> 24:23.669
Next is Rachel.

24:23.670 --> 24:27.006
Yeah, Joel meant
so much to so many of us.

24:27.007 --> 24:28.966
Can't hear you.

24:28.967 --> 24:31.135
Can you take him, please?

24:31.136 --> 24:33.096
Yeah. Okay, here we go.

24:40.854 --> 24:43.648
I said that Joel meant
so much to so many of us.

24:44.816 --> 24:46.067
But he wasn't the only one.

24:47.319 --> 24:49.112
I lost my sister that day.

24:50.113 --> 24:52.240
A lot of people in here buried family.

24:52.824 --> 24:55.660
And now, you wanna send, what,
you're saying 16 of our best?

24:57.746 --> 25:00.247
Well, while they're gone, who's gonna be
on the wall if Raiders come?

25:00.248 --> 25:02.708
A wall that's barely mended.

25:02.709 --> 25:05.879
And none of you up there can
promise us that all 16 will come back.

25:06.505 --> 25:10.550
So, my heart is with you, Tommy and Ellie.

25:11.551 --> 25:13.887
We are too hurt, and it is too soon.

25:15.138 --> 25:16.556
Thank you, Rachel.

25:20.727 --> 25:22.187
Next is Carlisle.

25:25.649 --> 25:29.861
I'll be quick.
'Cause this one's simple to me.

25:30.862 --> 25:33.782
People came and killed Joel.

25:34.950 --> 25:37.327
So, why wouldn't we wanna
take our vengeance?

25:38.328 --> 25:41.122
Well, because we're not supposed to.

25:42.874 --> 25:45.502
Forgive and be forgiven.

25:46.127 --> 25:48.713
No grudges. No revenge.

25:49.297 --> 25:50.840
And I'm not even a Christian.

25:51.258 --> 25:53.676
I've always seen the wisdom in that.

25:53.677 --> 25:58.098
That's what separates us from the Raiders
and the murderers.

25:59.182 --> 26:00.809
Our capacity for mercy.

26:01.977 --> 26:04.062
Those sons of bitches
don't deserve our mercy.

26:05.522 --> 26:06.981
Well, of course they don't deserve it.

26:06.982 --> 26:09.359
- That's what makes it mercy.
- Well, to hell with that.

26:10.402 --> 26:12.152
And to hell with you
for saying it, Carlisle.

26:12.153 --> 26:13.320
- Seth, sit down.
- No.

26:13.321 --> 26:15.406
- You're not on the list.
- No!

26:15.407 --> 26:17.534
What the hell
are we all talking about here?

26:19.619 --> 26:21.120
It's not fair.

26:21.121 --> 26:23.122
What, we gotta forgive everybody
when they show up

26:23.123 --> 26:25.082
and piss in our eye?

26:25.083 --> 26:26.876
They came into our house.

26:27.460 --> 26:29.296
They took one of ours.

26:30.046 --> 26:34.758
My God, somebody shoots your brother,
you wanna take the locks off your doors?

26:34.759 --> 26:35.885
Grow up!

26:36.636 --> 26:38.763
You idiots, they'll come back.

26:39.598 --> 26:42.309
They'll come back
because we didn't make 'em pay.

26:43.018 --> 26:45.395
And when they come back,
they'll be laughing.

26:47.606 --> 26:49.149
And you'll all deserve it.

26:50.525 --> 26:53.987
Bunch of goddamn victims.

27:08.501 --> 27:09.502
Ellie?

27:29.356 --> 27:31.315
I normally don't write things down

27:31.316 --> 27:33.776
because I normally
don't think before I talk,

27:33.777 --> 27:36.820
which has gotten me
in trouble before, a lot,

27:36.821 --> 27:40.241
and it's cost me in ways
that sometimes couldn't be undone.

27:41.076 --> 27:45.580
But I can't afford that right now,
because I know what I'm asking is a lot.

27:46.373 --> 27:49.249
I'm asking us to risk
more people and resources,

27:49.250 --> 27:51.293
and at the worst possible time.

27:51.294 --> 27:55.464
And I want everyone to know,
it's not because I want revenge.

27:55.465 --> 27:57.841
It's not. It's not about revenge.

27:57.842 --> 28:00.720
What I want is what you
used to give people.

28:01.805 --> 28:03.306
I want justice.

28:04.641 --> 28:08.060
Because it's either that,
or we do nothing.

28:08.061 --> 28:11.146
That's what everyone else
out there is going to do for us.

28:11.147 --> 28:12.523
Nothing.

28:12.524 --> 28:15.275
A whole world of people
who won't lift a finger

28:15.276 --> 28:18.196
if something bad happens to me or you.

28:19.781 --> 28:21.574
We have a word for these people.

28:22.367 --> 28:24.159
They're called strangers.

28:24.160 --> 28:26.995
Well, I don't think that
we're strangers to each other.

28:26.996 --> 28:29.498
And I want to know
that I can count on you.

28:29.499 --> 28:31.792
And I swear, if someone hurts any of you

28:31.793 --> 28:35.004
or the people you love,
you can count on me.

28:35.630 --> 28:37.632
That's what holds all this together.

28:38.800 --> 28:41.344
Not potluck dinners
or New Year's Eve dances.

28:42.345 --> 28:45.055
Definitely not a wall,
because that thing got busted through.

28:45.056 --> 28:46.975
But Jackson is still here.

28:50.311 --> 28:52.396
I'll accept whatever the council decides.

28:52.397 --> 28:55.567
But I am asking you, please,

28:56.901 --> 28:59.612
do what it takes to see
that justice is done.

29:01.322 --> 29:04.576
Not for me. Not even for Joel.

29:05.827 --> 29:10.874
I am asking you, please, do it for us.

29:15.795 --> 29:16.963
Thank you.

29:26.389 --> 29:31.351
The council will now vote on the proposal
to send a party of 16 citizens to Seattle

29:31.352 --> 29:34.939
to find the people who killed Joel
and execute them.

29:57.420 --> 29:59.047
Amy-Beth?

30:03.259 --> 30:04.260
Yes.

30:06.262 --> 30:07.263
No.

30:08.973 --> 30:10.099
Yes.

30:12.477 --> 30:13.603
No.

30:15.271 --> 30:16.272
No.

30:17.857 --> 30:18.858
Yes.

30:20.568 --> 30:21.611
No.

30:23.905 --> 30:24.948
No.

30:26.366 --> 30:27.492
No.

30:28.952 --> 30:29.994
No.

30:32.080 --> 30:33.331
No.

30:36.167 --> 30:39.921
The vote is 8 to 3.
The proposal is rejected.

30:45.677 --> 30:47.178
Adjourned.

31:12.287 --> 31:14.497
Here we go, nine. Here we go.

31:16.958 --> 31:17.959
Grab the ball!

31:19.043 --> 31:20.295
Attaboy, nine!

31:22.422 --> 31:23.839
Oh, shit.

31:23.840 --> 31:25.717
I didn't know you were a fan.

31:26.509 --> 31:29.136
Hell, yeah! I had Tigers season tickets.

31:29.137 --> 31:30.470
Get in the game, Charlie.

31:30.471 --> 31:33.307
This actually isn't that far off
from the '03 squad.

31:33.308 --> 31:35.475
Louie, stand up! Stand up!

31:35.476 --> 31:38.688
You want a beer? I get them from Marshall.

31:51.659 --> 31:54.037
I spotted you in the crowd
at the meeting today.

31:55.371 --> 31:56.372
Yeah.

31:57.624 --> 31:59.875
And I thought to myself,

31:59.876 --> 32:02.420
she's probably been extra busy
these last few weeks.

32:03.421 --> 32:04.796
Brutal.

32:04.797 --> 32:08.551
And I'm supposed to see a shrink myself,
you know, to process it all, it's...

32:09.135 --> 32:10.136
I'm the only one here.

32:10.970 --> 32:14.222
- So, what do you do, then?
- Oh, well, I'm an alcoholic.

32:14.223 --> 32:16.642
And I smoke as much weed as I can.

32:16.643 --> 32:18.436
You know, complete fuckin' disaster.

32:19.479 --> 32:21.564
But you're not here
'cause you're worried about me.

32:21.981 --> 32:24.608
Two outs, guys, two outs. Look alive!

32:24.609 --> 32:25.818
I don't know.

32:28.613 --> 32:30.073
You see things that others don't.

32:32.158 --> 32:35.035
I'm nervous she's gonna do
somethin' stupid.

32:35.036 --> 32:36.870
What, you didn't believe her speech?

32:36.871 --> 32:39.540
- Did you?
- Course not. She's a liar.

32:40.458 --> 32:42.668
Well, there's a difference
between lyin' and being a liar.

32:42.669 --> 32:45.254
Oh, I know. And that one? Liar.

32:46.089 --> 32:49.258
There was maybe one person
she told the truth to, and he's...

32:51.844 --> 32:53.680
But we can agree to disagree about that.

32:55.390 --> 32:59.643
What matters is you're afraid.
So, let's talk about it.

32:59.644 --> 33:02.021
Okay. Free of charge.

33:05.191 --> 33:08.444
I just don't want her to go down
the same paths that Joel did.

33:11.406 --> 33:13.741
Comin' up with justifications and such.

33:15.868 --> 33:18.246
All he was really doin' was lashin' out.

33:18.830 --> 33:21.833
So, you think she might have
learned that behavior from him?

33:24.085 --> 33:25.585
There it is! Keep it up.

33:25.586 --> 33:27.922
Turns out nurture can only do this much.

33:28.548 --> 33:30.507
The rest is nature.

33:30.508 --> 33:33.177
If she's on a path,
it's not one that Joel put her on.

33:34.470 --> 33:36.054
No. No.

33:36.055 --> 33:39.600
I think they were walking side by side
from the very start.

33:42.979 --> 33:44.230
Tommy, I get it.

33:45.189 --> 33:48.150
You inherited her,
and you wanna keep her out of trouble.

33:48.151 --> 33:50.987
Take it from a psychotherapist
of 40 years.

33:51.988 --> 33:53.364
Some people just...

33:57.493 --> 33:59.829
Some people just can't be saved.

34:28.274 --> 34:30.568
- Who is it?
- Dina.

34:34.489 --> 34:35.490
Hey.

34:38.076 --> 34:39.785
I'm just going to bed.

34:39.786 --> 34:42.997
No, I don't think
that is where you're going.

34:48.628 --> 34:51.464
- Are you alone?
- I'm alone.

35:00.014 --> 35:01.306
Get in.

35:01.307 --> 35:03.725
Oh, Christ.

35:03.726 --> 35:05.310
Please don't try and talk me out of this.

35:05.311 --> 35:06.896
You think that's why I'm here?

35:07.939 --> 35:10.733
So, what's your plan?

35:12.235 --> 35:14.153
Go to Seattle and kill Abby.

35:14.654 --> 35:15.696
What route?

35:17.031 --> 35:18.198
Northwest.

35:18.199 --> 35:21.660
And is that all guns, or do you
have medical supplies in there?

35:21.661 --> 35:22.745
No?

35:24.038 --> 35:26.498
Well, better not land weird on an ankle

35:26.499 --> 35:30.001
or get a fever on your
well-charted path "northwest."

35:30.002 --> 35:31.963
Okay, so what am I supposed to do?

35:38.594 --> 35:41.513
Stay off the highways.
Steer clear of cities or settlements.

35:41.514 --> 35:43.557
First stage
is through the national forest.

35:43.558 --> 35:46.935
Once we're out,
we follow the Snake River Canyon,

35:46.936 --> 35:48.520
then break off through
the Snoqualmie Pass.

35:48.521 --> 35:49.896
Snoqualmie?

35:49.897 --> 35:52.440
Yeah. Snoqualmie.

35:52.441 --> 35:55.819
Approach Seattle from the east,
then reassess based on what we find.

35:55.820 --> 35:58.572
Provisions. Travel light, but smart.

35:58.573 --> 36:00.615
Winter coats for beds,
jackets for blankets.

36:00.616 --> 36:02.951
First aid kits, batteries, bear spray.

36:02.952 --> 36:04.954
Now, handguns.
What are you bringing?

36:07.165 --> 36:09.041
- Is that Joel's?
- Mm-hm.

36:10.626 --> 36:12.210
So, that's what
you're gonna kill her with?

36:12.211 --> 36:14.337
- Fuckin' right.
- Then, save it for that.

36:14.338 --> 36:15.840
It's slow and kicks like hell.

36:18.217 --> 36:20.887
Really? Shoot your damn ass off?

36:21.679 --> 36:23.346
I've heard that before.

36:23.347 --> 36:25.849
We'll want at least 100 shells apiece,
plus 50 rifle rounds.

36:25.850 --> 36:28.393
Bring any long gun you want,
as long as it's scoped.

36:28.394 --> 36:31.229
Chlorine tablets, a pan,
and something to keep Shimmer dry.

36:31.230 --> 36:32.898
- Just Shimmer?
- Yeah.

36:32.899 --> 36:34.733
We share a horse. Fewer resources.

36:34.734 --> 36:38.362
Everything else is what you'd figure,
except this.

36:39.822 --> 36:40.865
Boots.

36:41.824 --> 36:44.367
Love the Converse.
Respect your consistency.

36:44.368 --> 36:46.578
But you're not crossing
open country in fuckin' Chucks.

36:46.579 --> 36:48.955
- I've done it before.
- No Chucks. Questions?

36:48.956 --> 36:51.625
Yeah, one. How the fuck
are we gonna get all of this?

36:51.626 --> 36:52.960
I know a guy.

36:53.961 --> 36:56.588
Oh, no. No, don't tell me
you told Jesse, please.

36:56.589 --> 36:58.882
Captain Wyoming? No.

36:58.883 --> 37:02.220
I love the man, but he's a little uptight
about rules and shit.

37:02.762 --> 37:04.512
Wear all the clothes you're gonna bring,

37:04.513 --> 37:06.014
fill your pockets with ammo.

37:06.015 --> 37:09.267
Everything else needs to fit inside
a holster or your backpack.

37:09.268 --> 37:12.355
We'll meet by the old east gate, 3:00 a.m.

37:13.064 --> 37:14.065
3:00 a.m.

37:15.691 --> 37:16.776
Hey.

37:19.820 --> 37:21.072
Thank you.

37:23.449 --> 37:25.825
You know, you could have just asked.

37:25.826 --> 37:27.954
No, I actually didn't know that.

37:30.790 --> 37:32.124
Now you do.

38:09.036 --> 38:10.413
Trade.

38:12.248 --> 38:14.125
It's better. Trade.

38:32.351 --> 38:34.311
How'd you get her out?

38:34.312 --> 38:36.604
Jeanine's night watch at the stables.

38:36.605 --> 38:38.690
She's sympathetic to our cause.

38:38.691 --> 38:39.983
"Our cause"?

38:39.984 --> 38:42.570
You're the one that gave
the "us" speech, not me.

38:44.655 --> 38:47.365
Saddlebags are filled with stuff
I had squirreled away.

38:47.366 --> 38:49.367
Two weeks' worth of hardtack, bandages,

38:49.368 --> 38:51.453
alcohol, meds, batteries.

38:51.454 --> 38:53.789
I'd come with you, but I caught
some friendly fire on New Year's Day.

38:54.498 --> 38:56.625
- You sure it was friendly?
- Jesus Christ.

38:57.168 --> 38:59.211
We got ten minutes
before a patrol comes by.

39:00.212 --> 39:01.380
Let's get you going.

42:54.321 --> 42:56.031
Okay, so...

42:56.657 --> 42:57.658
F.

42:58.242 --> 42:59.243
F.

43:01.996 --> 43:03.621
- Fleetwood Mac.
- Nope.

43:03.622 --> 43:04.789
What?
What do you mean, "no"?

43:04.790 --> 43:06.541
- It's my opinion.
- Yeah, well,

43:06.542 --> 43:09.795
your opinion is wrong
because Frank Zappa exists.

43:12.006 --> 43:14.383
Okay, so, G.

43:15.092 --> 43:16.134
Green Day.

43:16.135 --> 43:18.429
No, you're wrong. It's Guns N' Roses.

43:23.601 --> 43:25.059
Ozzy Osbourne.

43:25.060 --> 43:27.312
Nice! Double points.

43:27.313 --> 43:30.815
So, L-M-N-O, P.

43:30.816 --> 43:33.360
Are you seriously gonna
make me do the entire alphabet?

43:33.986 --> 43:36.530
We don't have to. I'm incredibly flexible.

43:37.656 --> 43:39.198
Lemme see, new topic.

43:39.199 --> 43:41.284
- Or silence.
- Got one.

43:41.285 --> 43:42.744
First person you killed.

43:42.745 --> 43:44.203
Jesus, really?

43:44.204 --> 43:46.123
Yeah, fun stories of childhood.

43:46.665 --> 43:50.960
Okay, well, the first one's too fucked up,
but I can tell you the second one.

43:50.961 --> 43:52.046
I accept.

43:53.631 --> 43:56.090
It was a little before Joel
and I got to Jackson.

43:56.091 --> 44:01.055
In Kansas City, he got jumped by this kid,
maybe just a couple years older than me.

44:02.056 --> 44:06.435
And I came up behind him,
raised my gun and, yeah.

44:07.811 --> 44:09.812
Sorry, Ellie.

44:09.813 --> 44:13.025
Interesting.
I shoot a guy, and you feel sorry for me?

44:14.026 --> 44:16.320
I'm just loyal like that.

44:17.696 --> 44:19.364
Let me know if you see any outcroppings

44:19.365 --> 44:21.366
- or spots with cover.
- Why?

44:21.367 --> 44:22.951
It looks okay.

44:30.876 --> 44:32.627
Holy shit, that came on fast.

44:32.628 --> 44:35.004
How the fuck did you know
that was gonna happen?

44:35.005 --> 44:37.257
- I'm a witch.
- Clearly.

45:02.616 --> 45:04.118
Well, good night.

45:05.119 --> 45:06.245
Night.

45:22.594 --> 45:24.471
Okay, but I have a stupid question.

45:31.103 --> 45:35.482
It's about New Year's Eve,
and, you know,

45:36.608 --> 45:38.026
the kiss.

45:41.196 --> 45:42.572
Okay.

45:42.573 --> 45:45.450
I mean, whatever, you were super high.

45:45.451 --> 45:47.160
And you were drunk.

45:47.161 --> 45:48.661
Right, so it doesn't mean anything,

45:48.662 --> 45:50.789
- if that's what you're asking.
- No, I know that.

45:51.623 --> 45:52.916
My question is,

45:54.668 --> 45:56.879
how would you rate it?

45:58.088 --> 46:00.965
- Scale of one to ten.
- No.

46:00.966 --> 46:03.259
Come on.

46:03.260 --> 46:07.014
You've kissed girls before.
You're gay, I'm not.

46:07.639 --> 46:10.476
I'm just curious.
I wanna know if I'm any good at it.

46:11.435 --> 46:12.978
One to ten.

46:15.731 --> 46:17.315
Okay, fine. Six.

46:17.316 --> 46:18.691
Fuck you, "six."

46:18.692 --> 46:21.778
- That's not bad.
- That sucks!

46:21.779 --> 46:23.237
What?

46:23.238 --> 46:25.073
For the record, I don't believe you.

46:26.366 --> 46:29.328
Well, you asked, and I told you.
I'm sorry.

46:30.537 --> 46:33.456
You can go back to Jesse.

46:33.457 --> 46:34.917
I already did.

46:35.876 --> 46:37.878
Well, there you have it.

46:49.139 --> 46:51.016
Does he ever strike you as sad?

46:52.142 --> 46:53.894
Jesse? Yeah.

46:56.313 --> 46:57.898
Has he ever told you why?

46:59.316 --> 47:00.317
No.

47:03.529 --> 47:05.989
But I think deep inside,
that's just how he is.

47:09.785 --> 47:12.746
- At least, I hope that's why.
- Why would you hope that?

47:17.751 --> 47:19.670
Well, because if it's not that,

47:21.380 --> 47:22.673
then it's me.

47:27.553 --> 47:29.471
Well, good night.

47:30.472 --> 47:31.598
Night.

47:41.483 --> 47:42.609
Ellie?

47:44.820 --> 47:46.613
I wasn't that high.

47:59.710 --> 48:02.254
- How much further?
- Close.

48:03.422 --> 48:05.590
Maybe ten miles?

48:05.591 --> 48:09.428
In theory, we'll come out
near Highway Five, just north of the city.

48:28.655 --> 48:30.073
He was running away.

48:32.117 --> 48:34.243
What's that symbol?

48:34.244 --> 48:36.246
I don't know, I've never seen it before.

48:48.592 --> 48:51.637
A lot of different calibers.
I don't think this was FEDRA.

48:53.764 --> 48:54.848
Dina.

48:56.558 --> 48:57.851
Dina?

48:59.102 --> 49:00.354
Move.

49:06.693 --> 49:07.694
You okay?

49:08.570 --> 49:09.571
It's just...

50:05.168 --> 50:06.253
Doing okay?

50:08.755 --> 50:12.217
Yeah, I'm sorry, it's just
that's never happened before.

50:13.802 --> 50:14.969
I think it was the smell.

50:14.970 --> 50:16.638
It wasn't easy to look at either.

50:20.183 --> 50:22.185
If this was fucking them,

50:22.769 --> 50:24.646
if Abby and her crew did this to people,

50:25.814 --> 50:27.190
to kids?

50:31.153 --> 50:32.362
Yeah.

50:36.116 --> 50:37.284
Let's go.

51:07.773 --> 51:09.191
We're close now.

51:38.970 --> 51:40.429
It's quiet.

51:40.430 --> 51:42.808
Yeah. Too quiet.

51:44.309 --> 51:47.270
- Curtis or Viper?
- Both, in all four movies.

51:50.774 --> 51:52.400
Nine more miles.

51:54.152 --> 51:55.445
Nine more.

52:19.594 --> 52:21.972
Fucking Seattle. Pretty.

52:24.933 --> 52:26.685
Plus, no one's shooting at us.

52:30.355 --> 52:32.107
I guess there aren't that many Wolves.

52:33.400 --> 52:35.360
There's about to be a whole lot less.

52:37.821 --> 52:38.988
Curtis or Viper?

52:38.989 --> 52:40.489
What?

52:40.490 --> 52:44.452
No, that was just me.
I was trying to sound like a badass.

52:47.038 --> 52:48.623
You don't need to try.

53:08.852 --> 53:10.395
Manny.

53:11.354 --> 53:12.606
Yeah, go ahead.

53:14.608 --> 53:16.150
We're moving up to the FOB.

53:16.151 --> 53:18.278
All clear between
checkpoint three and five?

53:22.032 --> 53:24.158
Told me to watch six and eight.

53:24.159 --> 53:26.786
Now, they want fuckin' three and five.

53:28.288 --> 53:29.788
Manny, you copy?

53:29.789 --> 53:32.792
Just give me a fuckin' second. Jesus.

53:37.464 --> 53:39.883
You're all good. You can move up.
